      "updated_at": "2026-07-21",
      "content": "# Antidetect Browsers & Proxies\n\n## What an antidetect browser is\n\nAn antidetect browser is an isolated browser profile with a stable device fingerprint.\nEach connected LinkedIn account lives in exactly one browser; LinkedIn always sees the\nsame \"device\" in the same location, which is what keeps automated activity looking like\nthe account's normal usage.\n\n## Browser lifecycle\n\nA browser is **created** (cloud-minted or bring-your-own), then **run** when work needs\nit and **stopped** when idle (automatically after ~15 minutes; see *Sync Windows &\nBrowser Auto-Suspend*). Deleting a browser removes the profile; the bound LinkedIn\naccount can be reconnected later through a new browser.\n\nIf a running browser becomes unhealthy (its LinkedIn tab dies, the profile crashes), the\nplatform marks it with an issue status and powers it off instead of leaving it running\nblind. Fix the underlying problem (most often the proxy), then run it again.\n\n## Proxies\n\n- **Cloud-minted browsers require a proxy.** You pick the country when creating; the\n  platform attaches a suitable proxy automatically.\n- **BYO browsers bring their own.** The vendor profile keeps whatever proxy it already\n  has; the platform does not attach one.\n\nChoose the proxy country to match where the account genuinely operates. A sudden country\nchange is a classic trigger for LinkedIn verification challenges.\n\n## Proxy troubleshooting\n\nTwo checks are available per browser:\n\n- **Connectivity check** verifies the proxy actually answers.\n- **Location check** verifies the proxy's real-world geo matches what is configured.\n\nIf LinkedIn does not load inside the browser, run the connectivity check first. A browser\nwhose proxy is dead cannot sync or act; parked work resumes automatically once the\nbrowser is healthy again.\n\n## Browser logs\n\nEvery browser keeps an event log (starts, stops, faults, health checks). Open the\nbrowser's drawer to inspect it when diagnosing \"why did this stop overnight\" questions."
